```

Also make sure you don't upload a production database, private uploads, or secret keys. Strapi may use SQLite locally, so we should preserve your local data rather than blindly upload database files.

## Step 3 — Create a separate GitHub repository

Open <Link url="https://github.com/new" title="GitHub — Create repository"/> and create a repository named **`developer-portfolio-strapi`**.

- Choose Public or Private. I'd recommend **Private** for now.
- Leave README, `.gitignore`, and license unchecked.

Then come back here and tell me when the repository is created. We'll initialize Git inside the Strapi folder, verify the files, commit, and push it safely.


